.TH TEKX 1 "November 2026" "tekx 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tekx \- typeset mathematics into accessible PDF and HTML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tekx
.RB [ \-E | \-P | \-M | \-S ]
.RB [ \-w ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.I file.tekx
.br
.B tekx
.BR pp | parse | eqn | set | pdf | html
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B tekx explain
.RI [ formula ...]
.br
.B tekx new
.I name
.br
.B tekx pkg
.BR new | add | install | verify | lock | list | remove | search | registry
.RI [ args ]
.br
.B tekx \-v
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tekx
reads a document written in the tekx language and writes a PDF 2.0 file that
conforms to PDF/UA\-2, WTPDF and PDF/A\-4 (PDF/A\-4f when it carries files).
Mathematics is written the way it is spoken:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sum k^2 for k from 1 to n = n(n + 1)(2n + 1)/6
integral of e^(\-x^2) dx from \-infinity to infinity = sqrt pi
limit of sin x / x as x approaches 0 = 1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Every formula is typeset with the font's OpenType MATH table, tagged with
MathML structure, given spoken alternative text, and given a linear copy text
that
.B tekx
reads back as the same formula.
.PP
The output file is
.I file.pdf
unless
.B \-o
says otherwise.
An output name ending in
.I .html
selects the web back end instead: the same document as HTML with MathML.
Nothing is printed on success, and nothing is written when there are errors.
.PP
The work is done by filters connected by text streams.
Each can be run alone; with no
.I file
it reads the standard input.
.TP
.B pp
macro preprocessor: comments,
.BR do \&...\& end ,
definitions, block and text macros; writes core tekx with
.B #line
markers.
.TP
.B parse
structure: writes the document tree, one node per line, nested by indentation.
.TP
.B eqn
mathematics: adds layout, MathML, speech and copy text to every formula.
.TP
.B set
typesetting: line breaking, hyphenation, pages, numbering and cross-references;
writes a page description.
.TP
.B pdf
device back end: subsets fonts and writes tagged PDF.
.TP
.B html
web back end: reads the tree after
.B eqn
and writes HTML with MathML.
.PP
Thus
.PP
.RS
.nf
tekx pp paper.tekx | tekx parse | tekx eqn | tekx set | tekx pdf >paper.pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
is the same as
.BR "tekx paper.tekx" .
.PP
.B tekx explain
shows how formulas are read: the grouping the parser chose, with every
implicit parenthesis written out, the speech, the copy text and the MathML.
It takes formulas as arguments, or one per line on the standard input.
.PP
.B tekx new
.I name
writes
.I name.tekx
and
.IR name.bib :
a paper to start from, with front matter, a theorem, a proof, citations and
an appendix.
.PP
.B tekx pkg
manages packages: shared notation, environments, macros and programs that a
document takes in with
.BR "use NAME [VERSION]" .
.B tekx pkg add
fetches a package from a directory, a git URL or a registry and pins its
version, source and SHA\-256 content hash in
.IR tekx.lock ;
.B tekx pkg install
reproduces exactly what the lock pins.
Every build verifies the hash of each package it uses.
See
.IR doc/packages.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-E
Stop after
.B pp
and write core tekx to the standard output.
.TP
.B \-P
Stop after
.B parse
and write the document tree.
.TP
.B \-M
Stop after
.B eqn
and write the tree with laid-out mathematics.
.TP
.B \-S
Stop after
.B set
and write the page description.
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Write the result to
.IR output ;
.B \-
means the standard output.
.TP
.B \-w
Watch: build, then build again whenever the document or one of its inputs
(sources, bibliographies, images, fonts, packages) changes.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.SH THE LANGUAGE
A short example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
title "On Primes"
author "Ada Lovelace"
date today

section Euler's product #euler

For $s > 1$,

    zeta(s) = prod_(p prime) 1/(1 \- p^(\-s))   #product

theorem "Euclid"
  There are infinitely many primes; see @product.
.fi
.RE
.PP
Blocks start with a keyword and take an indented body:
.BR section ,
.BR theorem ,
.BR lemma ,
.BR definition ,
.BR proof ,
.BR abstract ,
.BR quote ,
lists, tables, code,
.BR contents ,
.BR references .
A line indented further than the text around it is display mathematics.
.B #label
marks a target and
.B @label
refers to it.
.B define
declares text macros, block macros, mathematical notation and new theorem-like
environments.
The full reference is
.IR doc/language.md ;
the formats between the stages are described in
.IR doc/machinery.md .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
The time used for
.B date today
and for the PDF's dates.
With it set, the same input always produces the same bytes.
.TP
.B TEKX_PATH
Directories, separated by colons, searched for packages when no
.I tekx.lock
is found beside the document or above it.
.TP
.B TEKX_REGISTRY
Package registries (directories or git URLs), separated by blanks, searched by
.B tekx pkg add
after the project's own.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the document has errors, 2 for usage errors and failures
such as an unreadable file.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are written to the standard error as
.PP
.RS
.IB file : line : column ": error: " message
.RE
.PP
with a suggestion where one can be made, for example
.IR "unknown label @strat; did you mean @start?" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Typeset a document:
.PP
.RS
.B tekx paper.tekx
.RE
.PP
See how a formula is understood:
.PP
.RS
.nf
echo \(aq$sum 1/k^2 for k from 1 to infinity$\(aq | tekx \-M \- | grep \-E \(aqspeech|linear\(aq
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eqn (1),
.BR troff (1),
.BR tex (1)
.SH STANDARDS
ISO 32000\-2 (PDF 2.0), ISO 14289\-2 (PDF/UA\-2), ISO 19005\-4 (PDF/A\-4),
WTPDF 1.0, MathML Core,
OpenType 1.9 MATH.
